---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility | Archytum" description="Archytum's commitment to an accessible website experience.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Accessibility" title="A site that works beyond one screen or input method." lede="Accessibility is part of the acceptance standard, not a launch-day add-on." />
  <article class="content">
    <h2>Our approach</h2>
    <p>Archytum aims to provide a website that is perceivable, operable, understandable, and robust. The site is designed for keyboard access, clear structure, visible focus, readable contrast, responsive layouts, reduced motion preferences, and meaningful labels.</p>
    <h2>Testing</h2>
    <p>Before launch, the site will receive automated and manual testing across current browsers and representative mobile and desktop layouts. Automated checks cannot replace manual keyboard, focus, content-order, zoom, and error-state review.</p>
    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>If you encounter an accessibility barrier, email <a href="mailto:blake@archytum.com">blake@archytum.com</a> and describe the page, issue, assistive technology if relevant, and the format or outcome you need. Do not include sensitive information.</p>
    <p class="article-meta">Last updated: September 28, 2026</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
